00:26:14.207 --> 00:26:15.529
Related ADRs:

377
00:26:15.809 --> 00:26:40.087
ADR-078 JDK 25 + virtual threads by default; ADR-079 Structured concurrency for fan-out (preview, wrapped); ADR-080 No per-thread caches, ScopedValue for context; ADR-081 Explicit limits per dependency and for CPU work; ADR-082 Reactive only for streaming and gateways.

378
00:26:41.437 --> 00:26:42.077
1.

379
00:26:42.357 --> 00:26:43.765
Context and Problem.

380
00:26:44.045 --> 00:27:00.813
The move to virtual threads on JDK 21 caused pinning stalls (p99 6 s), +400 MB from per-thread caches, a downstream overload once the thread ceiling was gone, and leaking fan-out tasks (§1.1).

381
00:27:01.093 --> 00:27:01.797
2.

382
00:27:02.077 --> 00:27:03.421
Goals or Non-Goals.

383
00:27:03.701 --> 00:27:18.591
Goals: high concurrency for I or O-bound services with simple blocking code; no pinning stalls; bounded memory per in-flight request; explicit limits on dependencies and CPU work; fan-outs that fail fast and never leak.

384
00:27:18.871 --> 00:27:28.791
Non-goals: rewriting existing reactive services; eliminating all synchronized (fine on JDK 25 when no I or O is involved).

385
00:27:30.141 --> 00:27:30.888
3.

386
00:27:31.168 --> 00:27:32.128
Requirements.

387
00:27:33.478 --> 00:27:34.822
Here is a quick table:

388
00:27:35.102 --> 00:27:36.574
ID, and Requirement.

389
00:27:36.854 --> 00:27:37.899
NFR-1:

390
00:27:38.179 --> 00:27:43.299
All services on JDK 25 with virtual threads for request handling.

391
00:27:43.579 --> 00:27:44.625
NFR-2:

392
00:27:44.905 --> 00:27:51.582
0 jdk.VirtualThreadPinned events 20 ms in load tests (JFR check in CI).

393
00:27:51.862 --> 00:27:52.929
NFR-3:

394
00:27:53.209 --> 00:28:00.547
Heap per in-flight request at most 50 KB (load-test measurement); no ThreadLocal caches of large objects.

395
00:28:00.827 --> 00:28:01.915
NFR-4:

396
00:28:02.195 --> 00:28:08.318
Every outbound dependency has a concurrency limit; CPU-bound work runs on a bounded pool.

397
00:28:08.598 --> 00:28:09.643
NFR-5:

398
00:28:09.923 --> 00:28:18.627
Fan-out endpoints: an error response within 50 ms of the first required failure; 0 subtasks alive after the response.

399
00:28:18.907 --> 00:28:19.995
NFR-6:

400
00:28:20.275 --> 00:28:26.526
Streaming endpoints use Reactive Streams backpressure or bounded buffers with an explicit drop policy.

