427
00:29:31.632 --> 00:29:32.827
Proposed design.

428
00:29:33.107 --> 00:29:44.349
JDK 25 base image, spring.threads.virtual.enabled=true, and JFR continuous recording with the pinning and contention events enabled.

429
00:29:44.629 --> 00:30:02.549
Concurrency limits in the platform HTTP or gRPC clients (Ch 17): a semaphore per dependency, Hikari pools sized from Little's law, and a bounded ThreadPoolExecutor for CPU-heavy tasks (cores threads, bounded queue, caller-runs or reject).

430
00:30:03.899 --> 00:30:18.619
Fan-out: a platform ParallelCalls helper wrapping StructuredTaskScope (preview enabled in the service), with required or optional groups, budgets from the request deadline, and ScopedValue propagation of the request context.

431
00:30:18.899 --> 00:30:22.675
It can switch to the final API without touching call sites.

432
00:30:22.955 --> 00:30:28.929
Context: request id, tenant, customer and deadline in ScopedValues bound by a filter.

433
00:30:29.209 --> 00:30:32.302
ThreadLocal-based caches are banned by a lint rule.

434
00:30:32.582 --> 00:30:33.414
Streaming:

435
00:30:33.694 --> 00:30:41.033
WebFlux for SSE or WebSocket endpoints, and Kafka consumers with bounded hand-off queues and pause or resume.

436
